    {k:"p", t:"For example, a class studies a service from a printed description. One learner explains a prayer's purpose; another prefers not to recite it. Both can complete the same comparison task. A pupil with a mobility difficulty uses pictures rather than visiting an inaccessible building. This is inclusive study: equal learning does not require identical bodily actions or a shared profession of faith."}
